{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'AnnotationAssertion\\\\(rdfs:label obo:CL_0007011|AnnotationAssertion\\\\(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000101|AnnotationAssertion\\\\(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000099|AnnotationAssertion\\\\(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000100|AnnotationAssertion\\\\(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000108|AnnotationAssertion\\\\(rdfs:label obo:CL_0008015|AnnotationAssertion\\\\(rdfs:label obo:CL_4047038|myenteric|Dogiel|enteric neuron|sensory neuron|interneuron|cholinergic neuron|nitrergic' src/ontology/cl-edit.owl\"","aggregated_output":"4766:# Class: obo:CL_0000099 (interneuron)\n4772:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000099 \"CNS interneuron\")\n4773:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000099 \"interneuron\")\n4784:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000100 \"motor neuron\")\n4787:# Class: obo:CL_0000101 (sensory neuron)\n4794:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000101 \"sensory neuron\")\n4801:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23749412\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000102 \"polymodal sensory neuron\")\n4807:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0444009442\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000103 \"A type of interneuron that has two neurites, usually an axon and a dendrite, extending from opposite poles of an ovoid cell body.\")\n4846:# Class: obo:CL_0000108 (cholinergic neuron)\n4853:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000108 \"cholinergic neuron\")\n4935:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:Basket_cell&oldid=951703880\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000118 \"Basket cells are inhibitory GABAergic interneurons of the brain. In general, dendrites of basket cells are free branching and contain smooth spines. Axons are highly branched. The branched axonal arborizations give rise to basket-like structures that surround the soma of the target cell. Basket cells form axo-somatic synapses, meaning their synapses target somas of other cells.\")\n5795:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000207 \"olfactory sensory neuron\")\n7224:# Class: obo:CL_0000397 (ganglion interneuron)\n7226:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000397 \"ganglion interneuron\")\n7259:# Class: obo:CL_0000402 (obsolete CNS interneuron)\n7261:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1016/B978-0-12-817424-1.00001-X\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000402 \"OBSOLETE. An interneuron that has its cell body in a central nervous system.\")\n7264:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000402 \"Interneurons are commonly described as being only found in the central nervous system. However, in CL we define 'interneuron' more broadly as any neuron that is neither a motor neuron nor a sensory neuron, regardless of its location, so we need this term to refer strictly to interneurons of the central nervous system.\")\n7265:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000402 \"obsolete CNS interneuron\")\n7287:# Class: obo:CL_0000406 (CNS short range interneuron)\n7289:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000406 \"CNS short range interneuron\")\n7315:# Class: obo:CL_0000410 (CNS long range interneuron)\n7317:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000410 \"CNS long range interneuron\")\n7996:# Class: obo:CL_0000498 (inhibitory interneuron)\n7998:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interneuron\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000498 \"An interneuron (also called relay neuron, association neuron or local circuit neuron) is a multipolar neuron which connects afferent neurons and efferent neurons in neural pathways. Like motor neurons, interneuron cell bodies are always located in the central nervous system (CNS).\")\n8000:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000498 \"inhibitory interneuron\")\n8243:# Class: obo:CL_0000528 (nitrergic neuron)\n8247:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000528 \"nitrergic neuron\")\n8263:# Class: obo:CL_0000531 (primary sensory neuron (sensu Teleostei))\n8266:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000531 \"primary sensory neuron (sensu Teleostei)\")\n8285:# Class: obo:CL_0000534 (primary interneuron (sensu Teleostei))\n8287:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:1842357\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000534 \"A primary neuron (sensu Teleostei) that is neither a sensory neuron or a motor neuron.\")\n8288:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000534 \"primary interneuron (sensu Teleostei)\")\n9200:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:mah\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1038/s41598-018-27692-8\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000626 \"A granule cell that has a soma located in an olfactory bulb granule cell layer. An olfactory granule cell is an interneuron that lacks an axon, makes reciprocal dendro-dendritic synapses with mitral cells and tufted cells and is involved in the fine spatio-temporal tuning of the responses of these principal olfactory bulb neurons to odors.\")\n9789:# Class: obo:CL_0000691 (stellate interneuron)\n9792:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000691 \"stellate interneuron\")\n9808:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"JB:jb\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17122314\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000693 \"An interneuron that has spider-like appearance with a small round soma, a large number (7-10) of short, smooth, or slightly beaded primary dendrites that give rise to only a few secondary branches, and a branched axon that establishes a dense axonal mesh with thin shafts.\")\n11444:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000847 \"ciliated olfactory sensory neuron\")\n11445:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000847 \"ciliated sensory neuron\")\n11452:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000848 \"microvillous olfactory sensory neuron\")\n11453:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000848 \"microvillous sensory neuron\")\n11461:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000849 \"crypt olfactory sensory neuron\")\n11462:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000849 \"crypt sensory neuron\")\n21710:# Class: obo:CL_0004001 (local interneuron)\n21712:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004001 \"An interneuron whose axon stays entirely within the gray matter region where the cell body resides.\")\n21716:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0004001 \"Local interneurons form the category of interneurons whose axon stays entirely within the gray matter region where the cell body resides (Swanson, 2003, p. 245; Bota and Swanson, 2007, Fig. 3).\")\n21717:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004001 \"local interneuron\")\n22386:# Class: obo:CL_0005000 (spinal cord interneuron)\n22388:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CL:CVS\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0005000 \"A CNS interneuron located in the spinal cord.\")\n22389:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0005000 \"Is_a interneuron, part_of UBERON:0002240.\")\n22390:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0005000 \"spinal cord interneuron\")\n22440:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15539490\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0005007 \"KA interneuron\")\n22491:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22118931\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23959957\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25729351\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26378583\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0005012 \"While the term 'multi-ciliated epithelial cell' refers to cells with multiple motile cilia, there are exceptions where epithelial cells may have multiple non-motile cilia. Examples include olfactory sensory neurons, which have non-motile cilia for sensory detection, and choroid plexus epithelial cells, which possess multiple non-motile cilia with transient motility during development. Multiciliated cells are essential for human health, and their dysfunction can lead to various diseases known as ciliopathies, such as primary ciliary dyskinesia. This condition affects the respiratory system, brain ventricles, and reproductive system, leading to chronic respiratory infections, hydrocephalus, and infertility\")\n22719:# Class: obo:CL_0007011 (enteric neuron)\n22724:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0007011 \"enteric neuron\")\n22945:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0008015 \"inhibitory motor neuron\"@en)\n23042:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0008029 \"Consider GABAergic neuron or inhibitory interneuron instead. Do note that not all GABAergic neurons are inhibitory (see PMID:12209121) and replacing inhibitory neuron with GABAergic neuron should be done with caution.\")\n23055:# Class: obo:CL_0008031 (cortical interneuron)\n23057:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008031 \"An interneuron that has its soma located in the cerebral cortex.\")\n23058:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0008031 \"cerebral cortex interneuron\")\n23059:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0008031 \"cortical interneuron\"@en)\n23064:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1038/s41593-018-0205-2\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008032 \"A GABAergic interneuron in human cortical layer 1 that has large rosehip-shaped axonal boutons and compact arborization.\")\n23205:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1016/B978-0-443-10321-6.00004-7\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Intrafusal_muscle_fiber&oldid=937508784\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008047 \"A skeletal muscle fiber that is part of a muscle spindle. These are specialized muscle fibers that serve as proprioceptors, detecting the amount and rate of change in length of a muscle. They are innervated by both sensory neurons and motor neurons (gamma and beta motorneurons, collectively referred to as fusimotor neurons).\")\n23226:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1101/2020.03.31.016972\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Betz_cell&oldid=977472330\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008049 \"A giant pyramidal neuron with a soma in layer Vb of the primary motor cortex that sends its axons down the spinal cord via the corticospinal tract, either synapsing directly with alpha motor neurons, or targeting interneurons in the spinal cord. In humans, Betz cells are the largest known in the central nervous system.\")\n23273:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29651049\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008061 \"A neuron that releases both gamma-aminobutyric acid and acetylcholine as vesicular neurotransmitters.  Examples include some types of striatal interneuron.\")\n23279:# Class: obo:CL_0009000 (sensory neuron of spinal nerve)\n23281:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:nv\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:pr\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009000 \"A sensory neuron of the spinal nerve that senses body position and sends information about how much the muscle is stretched to the spinal cord.\")\n23282:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0009000 \"spinal sensory neuron\")\n23283:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0009000 \"sensory neuron of spinal nerve\")\n24590:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31110133\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:5042759\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0010010 \"A GABAergic interneuron that is located in the molecular layer of the cerebellum. This cell receives excitatory inputs primarily from parallel fibers and plays a crucial role in feed-forward inhibition by suppressing the activity of Purkinje cells and modulating the output of the cerebellar cortex. The stellate cell is part of the local circuitry that contributes to the fine-tuning of motor coordination and a regulator of cerebellar blood flow via neurovascular coupling.\")\n24599:# Class: obo:CL_0010011 (cerebral cortex GABAergic interneuron)\n24601:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dos\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0010011 \"A GABAergic interneuron whose soma is located in the cerebral cortex.\")\n24602:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0010011 \"cerebral cortex GABAergic interneuron\")\n24670:# Class: obo:CL_0011000 (dorsal horn interneuron)\n24672:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:nv\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0011000 \"A CNS interneuron located in the dorsal horn of the spinal cord.\")\n24673:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0011000 \"dorsal spinal cord interneuron\")\n24674:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0011000 \"dorsal horn interneuron\")\n24711:# Class: obo:CL_0011005 (GABAergic interneuron)\n24713:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:CellBLAST\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:nv\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29724907\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0011005 \"An interneuron that uses GABA as a vesicular neurotransmitter.  These interneurons are inhibitory\")\n24714:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0011005 \"GABAergic inhibitory interneuron\")\n24716:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0011005 \"GABAergic interneuron\")\n24722:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:nv\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18677503\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:2273099\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0011006 \"A cerebellar interneuron characterized by a spindle-shaped or triangular soma, parasagittally oriented and located at the border between the granular layer and the Purkinje cell layer. The Lugaro cell extends dendrites predominantly in the parasagittal plane, forming synaptic interactions with basket, stellate, and Golgi cells. Its axonal projections extend upward into the molecular layer, where they form a parasagittal plexus and emit long transverse collaterals that run parallel to the long axis of the cerebellar folia. The Lugaro cell is capable of co-releasing GABA and glycine, as evidenced by the expression of glutamate decarboxylase (GAD65/67) and the glycine transporter GlyT2.\")\n24974:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:NV\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12771169\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0011104 \"A type of interneuron in the retinal inner nuclear layer which\n24984:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:NV\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12771169\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0011105 \"A type of interneuron in the retinal inner nuclear layer which\n24993:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:NV\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12771169\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0011106 \"A type of interneuron in the retinal inner nuclear layer which\n25525:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10377365\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10934256\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21925242\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:2329464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25374536\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25876458\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29651049\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37905876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020008 \"A large aspiny interneuron of the striatum that serves as the principal intrinsic source of acetylcholine while simultaneously releasing GABA. It is defined by coexpression of cholinergic markers (ChAT and VAChT/Slc18a3) and GABAergic markers (GAD65/Gad2 and VGAT/Slc32a1) (Lozovaya et al., 2018). This MGE-derived neuron maintains Lhx6 expression associated with dual-transmitter identity (Fragkouli et al., 2009; Marin et al., 2000). Morphologically, it possesses a large soma (20–50 μm diameter), 2–4 thick aspiny dendrites extending radially ~1 mm, and locally ramified axons with hundreds of thousands of varicosities (Wilson et al., 1990; Lim et al., 2014).\")\n25527:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10377365\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25876458\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29651049\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37905876\") terms:description obo:CL_0020008 \"Although they constitute only 1–3% of all striatal neurons, these interneurons form a major modulatory hub, integrating cortical, thalamic, and dopaminergic inputs and shaping striatal output dynamics (Gonzales & Smith, 2015; Wegman et al., 2024). Electrophysiologically, the neuron exhibits tonic autonomous firing at 3–10 Hz, broad action potentials, and a prominent hyperpolarization-activated inward current (Ih) (Bennett & Wilson, 1999; Goldberg & Reynolds, 2011). Functionally, it modulates corticostriatal and thalamostriatal synaptic transmission, dopamine release, and spiny projection neuron excitability through co-transmission of acetylcholine and GABA (Lozovaya et al., 2018; Wegman et al., 2024). This dual inhibitory and modulatory signaling underlies context-dependent control of synaptic plasticity, action selection, and reinforcement learning (Gonzales & Smith, 2015; Lozovaya et al., 2018).\")\n28798:# Class: obo:CL_1001434 (olfactory bulb interneuron)\n28800:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18603310\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_1001434 \"A neuron residing in the olfactory bulb that serve to process and refine signals arising from olfactory sensory neurons\")\n28801:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_1001434 \"olfactory bulb interneuron\")\n28832:# Class: obo:CL_1001451 (sensory neuron of dorsal root ganglion)\n28834:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MP:0004297\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_1001451 \"A sensory neuron of the dorsal root ganglia that senses body position and sends information about how much the muscle is stretched to the spinal cord.\")\n28836:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_1001451 \"sensory neuron of dorsal root ganglion\")\n28902:# Class: obo:CL_1001561 (vomeronasal sensory neuron)\n28905:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_1001561 \"vomeronasal sensory neuron\")\n28933:# Class: obo:CL_1001569 (hippocampal interneuron)\n28935:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:pr\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_1001569 \"An interneuron with a soma found in the hippocampus.\")\n28937:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_1001569 \"hippocampal interneuron\")\n29505:# Class: obo:CL_2000023 (spinal cord ventral column interneuron)\n29507:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:TermGenie\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_2000023 \"Any interneuron that is part of a spinal cord ventral column.\")\n29511:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_2000023 \"spinal cord ventral column interneuron\")\n29543:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32990595\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:8915580\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_2000027 \"A GABAergic inhibitory interneuron located in the molecular layer of the cerebellar cortex. It projects axons that form specialized synaptic structures around Purkinje cells, including pericellular baskets, which wrap around the Purkinje cell soma, and the pinceau: a brush-like terminal that contacts the initial segment of the Purkinje cell axon. The basket cell modulates Purkinje cell activity through both chemical (GABAergic) and non-synaptic (ephaptic) mechanisms. It is arranged in sagittal rows that align with Purkinje cell zones, contributing to the cerebellum's modular and topographically organized architecture. It plays an essential role in regulating motor coordination and potentially cognitive functions.\")\n30267:# Class: obo:CL_3000003 (sympathetic cholinergic neuron)\n30273:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_3000003 \"sympathetic cholinergic neuron\")\n30276:# Class: obo:CL_3000004 (peripheral sensory neuron)\n30278:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:CellBLAST\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30096314\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31554486\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35858549\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Sensory_neuron\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.britannica.com/science/sensory-neuron\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK539846/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_3000004 \"A neuron type that is located in a peripheral nervous system and it transmits sensory information from the peripheral (PNS) to the central nervous system (CNS). A sensory neuron converts physical (light, sound, touch) or chemical (such as taste and smell) stimuli into an electrical signal through a process known as sensory transduction. The function of a sensory neuron is to carry informations from the external environment and internal body conditions to the central nervous system for further processing.\")\n30282:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Sensory_neuron\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_3000004 \"Typically, a sensory neuron has a pseudounipolar morphology.\")\n30283:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_3000004 \"peripheral sensory neuron\")\n30359:# Class: obo:CL_4023007 (L2/3 bipolar VIP GABAergic interneuron (Mmus))\n30361:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4023007 \"L2/3 bipolar VIP interneuron (Mus)\")\n30362:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26420784\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023007 \"A VIP GABAergic cortical interneuron with bipolar morphology, with a soma found in L2/3. L2/3 bipolar VIP cells have extending axons across all layers (with preferences for layers II/III and Va) and a dendritic tree that is vertically more restricted than deeper layer VIP cells and extend fewer dendrites into the layers outside their home layer (location of soma). L2/3 bipolar VIP cells have great variability in firing patterns, though most are continuous adapting. L2/3 bipolar VIP cells are more depolarized in their resting state, had less fast rectification, and had smaller after hyperpolarization than deeper VIP cells.\")\n30366:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023007 \"L2/3 bipolar VIP GABAergic interneuron (Mmus)\")\n30397:# Class: obo:CL_4023010 (alpha7 GABAergic cortical interneuron (Mmus))\n30399:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4023010 \"A7 interneuron\")\n30400:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30413647\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33184512\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023010 \"A GABAergic cortical interneuron that is strongly labelled for α7 nAChRs. These cells have soma found in L1 and have multipolar dendrites with vertically descending axonal collaterals that project deep into the column, usually branching and terminating in L5A.\")\n30404:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1101/2020.10.19.343129\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30413647\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33184512\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4023010 \"Unlike typical Lamp5 electrophysiology, A7 cells have Vip- and Sst-like firing properties, with active depolarizing hump at near-threshold membrane potentials, and  larger hyperpolarization sag, stronger burst, and rebound firing. A7 cells have a transcriptomics signature that looks like Lamp5 GABAergic interneuron.\")\n30405:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023010 \"alpha7 GABAergic cortical interneuron (Mmus)\")\n30412:# Class: obo:CL_4023011 (lamp5 GABAergic interneuron)\n30414:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4023011 \"Lamp5 interneuron\")\n30419:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023011 \"lamp5 GABAergic interneuron\")\n30445:# Class: obo:CL_4023014 (L5 VIP GABAergic interneuron (Mmus))\n30447:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4023014 \"L5 VIP interneuron (Mus)\")\n30448:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26420784\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26612957\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023014 \"A VIP GABAergic cortical interneuron with a soma found in L5. L5 VIP cells have mostly local morphology with some deep-projecting axons. They show only moderate resistance, comparable to that of sst subclass and unlike typical VIP subclass cells that tend to show high input resistance. L5 VIP cells show particularly low resting membrane potential.\")\n30452:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023014 \"L5 VIP GABAergic interneuron (Mmus)\")\n30459:# Class: obo:CL_4023015 (sncg GABAergic interneuron)\n30461:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4023015 \"sncg interneuron\")\n30466:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023015 \"sncg GABAergic interneuron\")\n30471:# Class: obo:CL_4023016 (VIP GABAergic interneuron)\n30473:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4023016 \"VIP interneuron\")\n30476:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33108272\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4023016 \"VIP interneuron\")\n30486:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023016 \"VIP GABAergic interneuron\")\n30493:# Class: obo:CL_4023017 (sst GABAergic interneuron)\n30495:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4023017 \"sst interneuron\")\n30499:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30001424\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4023017 \"SOM+ inhibitory interneuron\")\n30501:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30001424\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4023017 \"somatostatin-expressing inhibitory interneuron\")\n30503:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023017 \"sst GABAergic interneuron\")\n30508:# Class: obo:CL_4023018 (pvalb GABAergic interneuron)\n30510:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4023018 \"pvalb interneuron\")\n30511:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27477017\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/9c63201d-bfd9-41a8-bbbc-18d947556f3d.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023018 \"A transcriptomically distinct GABAergic interneuron with a soma located in the pallium. These neurons express Parvalbumin.\")\n30515:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_4023018 \"Historically this term was used to refer to all Pvalb expressing GABAergic interneurons, but transcriptomic classification separates out some Pvalb expressing GABAergic interneurons as sibling classes (e.g. Pvalb chandelier).  We follow the transcriptomic classifications.\")\n30516:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023018 \"pvalb GABAergic interneuron\")\n30523:# Class: obo:CL_4023019 (L5/6 cck, VIP GABAergic interneuron (Mmus))\n30525:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33184512\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023019 \"A VIP GABAergic cortical interneuron that expresses cck. L5/6 cck cells have soma found mainly in L5 and L6 and have large axonal arborization.\")\n30529:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023019 \"L5/6 cck, VIP GABAergic interneuron (Mmus)\")\n30534:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:13933877\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:139469\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersion:Gamma_motor_neuron&oldid=906640465\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023020 \"A gamma motor neuron that innervates dynamic nuclear bag fibers (bag1 fibers) and enhances the sensitivities of Ia sensory neurons. They alter muscle spindle sensitivity and increases its discharge in response to velocity of muscle length (rather than just magnitude).\")\n30548:# Class: obo:CL_4023022 (canopy lamp5 GABAergic cortical interneuron (Mmus))\n30550:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4023022 \"canopy lamp5 interneuron\")\n30551:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30413647\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023022 \"A Lamp5 GABAergic cortical interneuron that has extended axons in the surface of L1. Canopy Lamp5 cells resemble neurogliaform cells in having elongated horizontal axonal arbors largely confined to L1; but the dendritic arbors are wider and have fewer branches, while the axon is less tortuous and extends further from the soma\")\n30554:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023022 \"canopy lamp5 GABAergic cortical interneuron (Mmus)\")\n30561:# Class: obo:CL_4023023 (L5,6 neurogliaform lamp5 GABAergic interneuron (Mmus))\n30563:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4023023 \"L5,6 NGC Lamp5 interneuron (Mus)\")\n30564:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26727548\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023023 \"A lamp 5 GABAergic cortical interneuron with neurogliaform morphology with a soma found in L5,6. L5,6 NGC lamp5 have deep afterhyperpolarization (AHP) but narrow action potentials (APs). Unlike other deep neurogliaform cells (which are caudal ganglionic eminence (CGE) derived), L5,6 NGC lamp5 cells are medial ganglionic eminence (MGE)-derived\")\n30568:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023023 \"L5,6 neurogliaform lamp5 GABAergic interneuron (Mmus)\")\n30576:# Class: obo:CL_4023024 (neurogliaform lamp5 GABAergic cortical interneuron (Mmus))\n30578:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4023024 \"NGC Lamp5 interneuron (Mus)\")\n30579:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27477017\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023024 \"A lamp5 GABAergic cortical interneuron with layer-adapting morphology. NGC lamp5 cells have a small round soma, short dendrites, and a wide dense axonal arbor that tends to establish a dense axonal mesh with high connection probability both to themselves and L2 pyramidal cells. NGC lamp5 cells have unique synaptic properties that distinguish them from other GABAergic interneurons, including the release of GABA to the extracellular space via volume transmission, and the ability to produce GABA-B responses in connected postsynaptic targets.\")\n30583:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023024 \"neurogliaform lamp5 GABAergic cortical interneuron (Mmus)\")\n30591:# Class: obo:CL_4023025 (long-range projecting sst GABAergic cortical interneuron (Mmus))\n30593:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26727548\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023025 \"A sst GABAergic cortical interneuron that is both an interneuron and a projecting neuron. They are found in all layers from upper L2/3 down to the bottom of L6. They have long-range projections, some with axons fading into white matter. These cells have low rebound potential, low hyperpolarization sag, and high variability in membrane time constant.\")\n30597:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023025 \"long-range projecting sst GABAergic cortical interneuron (Mmus)\")\n30616:# Class: obo:CL_4023027 (L5 sst T-Martinotti interneuron (Mmus))\n30618:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4023027 \"L5 T Martinotti sst interneuron (Mus)\")\n30619:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28254942\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29326172\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023027 \"A sst GABAergic cortical interneuron with a soma found in L5 and possesses 'T-shaped' Martinotti morphologies with local axonal plexus in L5a and translaminar axons restricted to the uppermost part of L1. They show low-threshold spiking patterns with strong rebound firing, and inhibit the L1 apical tuft of nearby pyramidal cells.\")\n30623:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023027 \"L5 sst T-Martinotti interneuron (Mmus)\")\n30632:# Class: obo:CL_4023028 (L5 non-Martinotti sst GABAergic interneuron (Mmus))\n30634:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4023028 \"L5 non-Martinotti sst interneuron (Mus)\")\n30635:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28254942\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29326172\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023028 \"A sst GABAergic cortical interneuron with a soma found in lower L5 with mostly local axonal arborization but with some sparse ascending axons. L5 non-Martinotti sst cells show somatic localization and local axon plexus in L5b and L5b/6 and substantial innervation of L3 and L4, and receive thalamic input from the ventral posteromedial nucleus and specifically target L4 neurons, avoiding L5 pyramidal cells. L5 non-Martinotti sst cells tend to show a higher input resistance and seem to be less stuttering.\")\n30639:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023028 \"L5 non-Martinotti sst GABAergic interneuron (Mmus)\")\n30658:# Class: obo:CL_4023030 (L2/3/5 fan Martinotti sst GABAergic interneuron (Mmus))\n30660:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4023030 \"L2/3/5 fan Martinotti sst interneuron (Mus)\")\n30661:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27225074\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27477017\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28254942\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29326172\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023030 \"A sst GABAergic cortical interneuron that has \\\"fanning-out' Martinotti morphology that is found in layer 2/3/5 of the cerebral cortex. They have local axon arbor and long ascending axons that spreads horizontally and arborizes significantly in L1.\")\n30666:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023030 \"L2/3/5 fan Martinotti sst GABAergic interneuron (Mmus)\")\n30674:# Class: obo:CL_4023031 (L4 sst Martinotti interneuron (Mmus))\n30676:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4023031 \"L4 sst interneuron (Mus)\")\n30677:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33184512\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023031 \"A sst GABAergic cortical interneuron with a soma found in lower L2/3 and upper 5, L4 Sst cells have Martinotti morphology with ascending axons but denser local axons and sparser ‘fanning-out’ projections to L1. L4 sst cells have smaller membrane time constant to calb2 (L2/3/5 fan Martinotti Cell) and non-zero afterdepolarization (ADP).\")\n30681:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023031 \"L4 sst Martinotti interneuron (Mmus)\")\n30703:# Class: obo:CL_4023034 (obsolete L2/3 pvalb-like sst GABAergic cortical interneuron (Mus musculus))\n30705:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33184512\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023034 \"OBSOLETE A sst GABAergic cortical interneuron transcriptomically between the sst and the pvalb families with a soma found in L2/3. Some L2/3 PV-like sst cells have Martinotti morphology while some have basket cell morphology. L2/3 PV-like sst cells have lower AP width and higher firing rate than typical Sst subclass cells. L2/3 PV-like sst cells have high maximum firing rate variability, with many classified as belonging to the pvalb subclass on the basis of electrophysiology.\")\n30711:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023034 \"obsolete L2/3 pvalb-like sst GABAergic cortical interneuron (Mus musculus)\")\n30724:# Class: obo:CL_4023036 (pvalb chandelier GABAergic interneuron)\n30727:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15378039\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27199673\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27477017\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023036 \"A transcriptomically distinct pvalb GABAergic interneuron located in the pallium. It is recognizable by the straight terminal axonal 'cartridges' of vertically oriented strings of synaptic boutons. Chandelier PV cells' boutons target exclusively the axon initial segment (AIS) of pyramidal cells, with a single cell innervating hundreds of pyramidal cells in a clustered manner.  These cells are fast-spiking.\")\n30736:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023036 \"pvalb chandelier GABAergic interneuron\")\n30917:# Class: obo:CL_4023053 (spinal interneuron synapsing Betz cell)\n30919:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1101/2020.03.31.016972\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18558853\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023053 \"A Betz cell that syanpses with spinal interneurons.\")\n30923:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023053 \"spinal interneuron synapsing Betz cell\")\n30962:# Class: obo:CL_4023057 (cerebellar inhibitory GABAergic interneuron)\n30964:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1101/2022.10.12.511898\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023057 \"A GABAergic interneuron whose soma is located in the cerebellar cortex.\")\n30966:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023057 \"cerebellar inhibitory GABAergic interneuron\")\n31011:# Class: obo:CL_4023063 (medial ganglionic eminence derived interneuron)\n31013:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4023063 \"MGE interneuron\")\n31014:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1101/2022.10.12.511898\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19709629\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023063 \"An interneuron that is derived from the medial ganglionic eminence. In mice and humans, it expresses LHX6 and SOX6.\")\n31016:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4023063 \"MGE interneuron\")\n31017:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023063 \"medial ganglionic eminence derived interneuron\")\n31022:# Class: obo:CL_4023064 (caudal ganglionic eminence derived interneuron)\n31024:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4023064 \"CGE interneuron\")\n31025:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20130169\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824663\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023064 \"An interneuron that is derived from the caudal ganglionic eminence.\")\n31027:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20130169\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4023064 \"caudal ganglionic eminence derived GABAergic interneuron\")\n31028:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20130169\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4023064 \"CGE interneuron\")\n31029:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824663\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4023064 \"CGE interneuron\")\n31032:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20130169\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4023064 \"CGE-derived interneuron\")\n31033:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023064 \"caudal ganglionic eminence derived interneuron\")\n31058:# Class: obo:CL_4023067 (obsolete Martinotti morphology L2/3 pvalb-like sst GABAergic cortical interneuron (Mus musculus))\n31060:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33184512\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023067 \"OBSOLETE A L2/3 pvalb-like sst GABAergic cortical interneuron (Mus musculus) that has Martinotti morphology.\")\n31066:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023067 \"obsolete Martinotti morphology L2/3 pvalb-like sst GABAergic cortical interneuron (Mus musculus)\")\n31077:# Class: obo:CL_4023069 (medial ganglionic eminence derived GABAergic interneuron)\n31079:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4023069 \"MGE gaba interneuron\")\n31080:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12637172\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023069 \"A GABAergic interneuron that develops from the medial ganglionic eminence and has migrated to the cerebral cortex.\")\n31082:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023069 \"medial ganglionic eminence derived GABAergic interneuron\")\n31086:# Class: obo:CL_4023070 (obsolete caudal ganglionic eminence derived GABAergic cortical interneuron)\n31088:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4023070 \"CGE gaba cortical interneuron\")\n31089:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20130169\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023070 \"OBSOLETE. A GABAergic cortical interneuron that develops from the caudal ganglionic eminence and has migrated to the cerebral cortex.\")\n31093:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4023070 \"CGE cortical interneuron\")\n31094:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_4023070 \"caudal ganglionic eminence derived GABAergic interneuron\n31095:and caudal ganglionic eminence derived interneuron are the same cell type. \n31099:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023070 \"obsolete caudal ganglionic eminence derived GABAergic cortical interneuron\")\n31102:# Class: obo:CL_4023071 (L5/6 cck GABAergic interneuron (Mmus))\n31104:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4023071 \"L5/6 cck interneuron (Mus)\")\n31105:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33184512\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023071 \"A GABAergic cortical interneuron that expresses cck. L5/6 cck cells have soma found mainly in L5 and L6 and have large axonal arborization.\")\n31109:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023071 \"L5/6 cck GABAergic interneuron (Mmus)\")\n31139:# Class: obo:CL_4023075 (L6 th sst GABAergic interneuron (Mmus))\n31141:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4023075 \"L6 th sst interneuron (Mus)\")\n31142:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22357664\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023075 \"A sst GABAergic cortical interneuron found in L6 that expresses tyrosine hydroxylase. L6 Th+ SST cells have mostly local axonal arborization within L6.\")\n31145:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4023075 \"L6 tyrosine hydroxylase positive sst expressing GABAergic cortical interneuron (Mus musculus)\")\n31147:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023075 \"L6 th sst GABAergic interneuron (Mmus)\")\n31157:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:Martinotti_cell&oldid=9947732\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023076 \"An interneuron that has Martinotti morphology. These interneurons are scattered throughout various layers of the cerebral cortex, sending their axons up to the cortical layer I where they form axonal arborization.\")\n31167:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18568015\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023077 \"A type of interneuron that has two clusters of dendritic branches that originate directly from the soma and extend in opposite directions and axons that form a plexus which spreads widely. Compared to bipolar neurons, bitufted neurons have branching that occur close to the soma.\")\n31174:# Class: obo:CL_4023078 (obsolete basket morphology L2/3 pvalb-like sst GABAergic cortical interneuron (Mus musculus))\n31176:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33184512\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023078 \"OBSOLETE A L2/3 pvalb-like sst GABAergic cortical interneuron (Mus musculus) that has basket morphology.\")\n31182:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023078 \"obsolete basket morphology L2/3 pvalb-like sst GABAergic cortical interneuron (Mus musculus)\")\n31485:# Class: obo:CL_4023118 (L5/6 non-Martinotti sst GABAergic interneuron (Mmus))\n31487:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4023118 \"L5/6 non-Martinotti sst interneuron (Mus)\")\n31488:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27477017\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023118 \"A sst GABAergic interneuron does not have Martinotti morphology with a soma found in L5/6 of the cerebral cortex.\")\n31491:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4023118 \"L5/6 non-Martinotti morphology sst expressing GABAergic cortical interneuron (Mus musculus)\")\n31494:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023118 \"L5/6 non-Martinotti sst GABAergic interneuron (Mmus)\")\n31521:# Class: obo:CL_4023121 (sst chodl GABAergic interneuron)\n31523:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4023121 \"sst chodl interneuron\")\n31524:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15845086\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31209381\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33372656\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/9c63201d-bfd9-41a8-bbbc-18d947556f3d.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023121 \"A transcriptomically distinct sst GABAergic interneuron that also expresses Chodl. These neurons are rare and correspond to the only known interneurons with long-range projection.\")\n31526:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33372656\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4023121 \"long-range GABAergic interneuron\")\n31527:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023121 \"sst chodl GABAergic interneuron\")\n31536:# Class: obo:CL_4023122 (oxytocin receptor sst GABAergic cortical interneuron)\n31538:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25303526\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023122 \"An interneuron located in the cerebral cortex that expresses the oxytocin receptor. These interneurons also express somatostatin.\")\n31543:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023122 \"oxytocin receptor sst GABAergic cortical interneuron\")\n31634:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15378039\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023159 \"An interneuron that has double bouquet morphology.\")\n31654:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9193142\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:Unipolar_brush_cell&oldid=1045937026\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023161 \"An excitatory glutamatergic interneuron found in the granular layer of the cerebellar cortex and also in the granule cell domain of the cochlear nucleus. Unipolar brush cells have a round or oval cell body with usually a single short dendrite that ends in a brush-like tuft of short dendrites unique to them known as dendrioles.\")\n31691:# Class: obo:CL_4023168 (somatosensory neuron)\n31693:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22865660\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023168 \"A neuron that is part of the somatic sensory system. Somatosensory neurons innervate the skin or integument to detect different types of thermal, chemical, and mechanical touch stimuli.\")\n31695:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023168 \"somatosensory neuron\")\n31706:# Class: obo:CL_4023170 (trigeminal sensory neuron)\n31710:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023170 \"trigeminal sensory neuron\")\n32565:# Class: obo:CL_4032001 (reelin GABAergic cortical interneuron)\n32567:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23803971\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4032001 \"A GABAergic interneuron located in the cerebral cortex that expresses reelin (rln).\")\n32571:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29904965\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4032001 \"rln GABAergic cortical interneuron\")\n32572:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4032001 \"reelin GABAergic cortical interneuron\")\n33579:# Class: obo:CL_4042001 (TAC3-positive striatal interneuron)\n33581:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32999462\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34727523\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4042001 \"A GABAergic interneuron that has its soma located in the striatum and that has an enriched expression of the genes TAC3 and LHX6.\")\n33584:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34727523\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4042001 \"TAC3 interneuron\")\n33585:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4042001 \"TAC3-positive striatal interneuron\"@en)\n33708:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34004146\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36007006\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824669\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/e4ddac12-f48f-4455-8e8d-c2a48a683437.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4042013 \"A transcriptomically distinct GABAergic interneuron marked by Lamp5 and Lhx6 expression, derived from the Medial Ganglionic Eminence (MGE), and located in the pallium.\")\n33723:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35418660\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4042014 \"A VIP GABAergic cortical interneuron with a soma located in L1-3 of some neocortex in Mmus. This neuron has a multipolar morphology with spiny dendrites concentrating on L1 of the cortex, and has a burst firing electrophysiological signature with highly dynamic dendritic spines.\")\n33732:# Class: obo:CL_4042015 (VIP-ChAT interneuron)\n33734:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30382198\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31754098\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32027647\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33301603\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4042015 \"A VIP GABAergic cortical interneuron expressing vasoactive intestinal polypeptide and choline acetyltransferase in the Mmus neocortex. This interneuron releases both γ-aminobutyric acid and acetylcholine.\")\n33737:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33301603\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4042015 \"VIP+/ChAT+ interneuron\")\n33738:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32027647\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4042015 \"VIP/ChAT interneuron\")\n33741:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30382198\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32027647\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33301603\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4042015 \"Work in the mouse barrel cortex and somatosensory cortex shows that a VIP-ChAT interneuron is predominantely located in L2/3 and more rarely in the deeper layers of the cortex (Dudai et al., 2021; Dudai et al., 2020). This neuronal type could be transcriptomically distinct as transcriptomic studies have identified VIP neurons expressing ChAT in a whole brain mouse transcriptomic study (Tasic et al., 2018).\")\n33742:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4042015 \"VIP-ChAT interneuron\"@en)\n33845:# Class: obo:CL_4042023 (striatal pthlh-expressing interneuron)\n33847:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30134177\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37292997\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4042023 \"A GABAergic interneuron expressing PTHLH and PVALB that has its soma in a striatum. This GABAergic interneuron type presents a spatial expression gradient of PVALB in the mouse striatum.\")\n33851:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37292997\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4042023 \"PTHLH +/PVALB+ interneuron\")\n33852:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37292997\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4042023 \"According to spatial transcriptomic data in the human striatum, pthlh-expressing interneurons are one of the most abundant population of interneurons in the striatum (Leonardo D. Garma, et al., 2024).\")\n33853:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4042023 \"striatal pthlh-expressing interneuron\"@en)\n33859:# Class: obo:CL_4042024 (striatal PTHLH MOXD1 expressing interneuron)\n33861:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30134177\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4042024 \"A pthlh-expressing interneuron that expresses MOXD1 and has its soma in a striatum.\")\n33864:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4042024 \"striatal PTHLH MOXD1 expressing interneuron\"@en)\n33878:# Class: obo:CL_4042026 (GABAergic interneuron of the anterior substantia nigra pars reticulata)\n33880:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36148148\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4042026 \"A GABAergic interneuron that has its soma in the anterior section of the substantia nigra pars reticulata. This GABAergic interneuron is characterized by the expression of Six3 and Foxp1 and it develops from Nkx6-2 expressing neuronal progenitors in the ventrolateral midbrain-diencephalon region.\")\n33884:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4042026 \"GABAergic interneuron of the anterior substantia nigra pars reticulata\"@en)\n33890:# Class: obo:CL_4042027 (GABAergic interneuron of the posterior substantia nigra pars reticulata)\n33892:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36148148\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4042027 \"A GABAergic interneuron that has its soma in the posterior section of the substantia nigra pars reticulata. This GABAergic interneuron is characterised by the expression of the transcription factors Pax5, Ctip2 and Pou6f2 and it develops from the ventrolateral r1 neuroepithelium expresing NKX61.\")\n33896:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4042027 \"GABAergic interneuron of the posterior substantia nigra pars reticulata\"@en)\n33922:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35578131\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4042030 \"A GABAergic interneuron located in the Purkinje layer of the cerebellar cortex. This GABAergic interneuron type has a distinct morphology, it presents a small cell soma near the Purkinje cell layer (PCL), dendrites that extend to the surface of the molecular layer, and beaded axons that make local synapses contacts within the molecular layer. A candelabrum cell is excited by mossy fibers and granule cells but inhibited by Purkinje cells, and it inhibits molecular layer interneurons, which leads to the disinhibition of Purkinje cells.\")\n33925:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35578131\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4042030 \"candelabrum interneuron\")\n33927:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35578131\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4042030 \"Candelabrum cells are the most abundant interneurons in the Purkinje cell layer and are present in all cerebellar lobules.\")\n33950:# Class: obo:CL_4042032 (PAX6 GABAergic interneuron)\n33952:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4042032 \"Pax6 interneuron\")\n33956:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4042032 \"PAX6 GABAergic interneuron\"@en)\n33977:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34061020\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4042034 \"An interneuron neuron characterized by the expression of calcitonin gene-related peptide (CGRP), a 37-amino acid neuropeptide. This neuron type is involved in nociception and pain modulation by facilitating the transmission of nociceptive signals from peripheral sensory nerve endings to central nervous system structures. This neuron type is found in the dorsal root ganglia (DRG) and trigeminal ganglion, and the spinal cord dorsal horn.\")\n33981:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34061020\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4042034 \"CGRP-expressing interneuron\")\n33987:# Class: obo:CL_4042035 (molecular layer interneuron)\n33989:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30742002\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33075461\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34616064\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38692278\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4042035 \"A type of cerebellar inhibitory GABAergic interneuron that is located in the molecular layer of the cerebellum. This cell type inhibits Purkinje cells and other molecular layer interneurons. This interneuron plays a crucial role in regulating cerebellar output through feedforward inhibition and is characterized by its fast-spiking properties.\")\n33993:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4042035 \"molecular layer interneuron\"@en)\n34008:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30131490\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30467465\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33742131\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4042037 \"A interneuron of the striatum expressing gamma-aminobutyric acid and somatostatin. This interneuron has a fusiform soma with a diameter between 9 - 25 µm, it has a long axon up to the length of 1mm. This neuron type displays a low threshold Ca2+ spike (LTS), a high input resistance, and the expression of long-lasting plateau potentials following depolarization from rest.\")\n34013:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30467465\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33742131\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4042037 \"Some striatal SST GABAergic neurons can co-release glutamate and generate excitation-inhibition responses in postsynaptic neurons. This interneuron type has the least dense dendritic branches in the striatum. In the dorsomedial striatum these neurons regulate the activity of striatal projection neurons.\")\n34034:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12593982\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12637172\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20130169\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK98190/\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4042039 \"Neurons derived from the caudal ganglionic eminence consist mostly of neurons populating the cortical layers of the brain and some subcortical areas such as the globus pallidus, the striatus and the hippocampus. Amongst neurons derived from the caudal ganglionic eminence there are cortical GABAergic neurons such as Pax6, Lamp5, VIP, sncg, GABAergic; in the hippocampus, mossy fibers, pyramidal neurons, granule neurons and interneurons; in the striatum and globus pallidus, medium spiny projection neurons.\")\n34208:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1038/s41575-020-0271-2\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1038/s41575-021-00561-y\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32152479\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34170401\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4047038 \"A multipolar neuron in the myenteric plexus of the gastrointestinal tract, characterized by a small to medium-sized cell body and multiple short dendrites.  This neuron exhibits fast excitatory postsynaptic potentials and can be classified into stubby, spiny and hairy subtypes based on dendritic morphology. (Brehmer, 2021)\")\n34211:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4047038 \"dogiel type I neuron\")\n34224:# Class: obo:CL_4047042 (type 1 myenteric plexus glia)\n34226:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19906678\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21865647\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26964064\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28066889\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33731961\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4047042 \"An enteric glial cell located within the myenteric ganglia of the gastrointestinal tract. This cell has a small somata and has very short, irregularly branched processes that surround neuron cell bodies, giving it a protoplasmic-like appearance. It plays crucial roles in modulating myenteric neuron activity, regulating oxidative stress, and influencing neuroinflammation and neurogenesis.\")\n34230:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4047042 \"type 1 myenteric plexus glia\")\n34246:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1002/glia.22876\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33731961\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35111752\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4047044 \"An enteric glial cell that has an elongated, fibrous morphology with long processes that run parallel to nerve fibers connecting enteric myenteric ganglia. This cell is located in the interganglionic fiber tracts of the enteric nervous system.\")\n34265:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1016/j.celrep.2023.112194\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29927320\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33731961\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35111752\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4047047 \"An enteric glial cell located within the ganglia of the enteric nervous system. This cell is characterized by it’s small somata and short, irregularly branched processes that surround neuronal cell bodies in the myenteric and submucosal ganglia. This cell plays important roles in modulating neuronal activity and neurogenesis in the gastrointestinal tract.\")\n34764:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38306414\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:/10.1101/2022.09.26.509561\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052037 \"A tuft cell that is part of the olfactory epithelium, characterized by a globular body and the expression of neurogranin (Nrgn) in mice. This cell plays a crucial role in allergen recognition and regulating olfactory stem cell proliferation via TRPM5-dependent ATP sensing and cysteinyl leukotriene production. Unlike nasal respiratory tuft cells, it has low to absent expression of taste receptors, including the G protein Gα gustducin, and rarely contacts olfactory sensory neurons directly.\")\n35280:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28261065\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:/10.1101/2023.08.29.554772\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072013 \"A type of dopaminergic interneuron located in the glomerular layer of the main olfactory bulb, characterized by the co-release of dopamine and GABA, and involved in modulating sensory input within olfactory circuits.\")\n35310:# Class: obo:CL_4072016 (NPY interneuron)\n35312:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19295167\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32376782\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072016 \"An interneuron that expresses neuropeptide Y (NPY) and is mainly located in cortical layers II–III and VI, as well as in various brain regions such as the medial geniculate and inferior colliculus. The NPY cell population is physiologically diverse, displaying a range of firing behaviors, including adapting, fast-spiking, and accelerating patterns.\")\n35315:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19295167\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4072016 \"NPY-expressing neocortical interneuron\")\n35316:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4072016 \"NPY interneuron\")\n35351:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21871477\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:2785663\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28790896\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33158870\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9662138\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072021 \"A specialised type of interneuron defined by the secretion of corticotropin-releasing hormone (CRH), a key peptide in activating the hypothalamic–pituitary–adrenal (HPA) axis during stress. It is primarily located in the paraventricular nucleus (PVN) of the hypothalamus, with additional presence in the hippocampus, piriform area, central amygdalar nucleus, Barrington’s nucleus, and inferior olivary complex (Peng et al., 2017).\")\n35359:# Class: obo:CL_4072022 (Lamp5 Lhx6 GABAergic interneuron (Homo sapiens))\n35361:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30382198\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36007006\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824669\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38712198\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072022 \"A Lamp5 Lhx6 GABAergic interneuron of Homo sapiens. The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: 'Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization', dataset: 'Supercluster: CGE-derived interneurons', Author Categories: 'CrossArea_subclass', Lamp5 Lhx6\")\n35365:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32999462\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4072022 \"Despite being clustered as CGE in this dataset, other studies suggest that the cell is of MGE origin because it expresses transcription factors such as LHX6 and NKX2-1, which are hallmark indicators of MGE-derived interneurons. Fate mapping experiments in mice have demonstrated that Lamp5+/Lhx6+ interneurons in both the hippocampus and neocortex arise from the MGE, and single-cell transcriptomic comparisons further show that primate neocortical Lamp5+/Lhx6+ cells closely resemble mouse hippocampal MGE-derived interneurons rather than classic CGE-derived types.\")\n35367:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4072022 \"Lamp5 Lhx6 GABAergic interneuron (Homo sapiens)\")\n35376:# Class: obo:CL_4072027 (sst GABAergic interneuron (Homo sapiens))\n35378:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4072027 \"sst interneuron (Homo sapiens)\")\n35379:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27477017\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33742131\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/9c63201d-bfd9-41a8-bbbc-18d947556f3d.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072027 \"A transcriptomically distinct GABAergic neuron located in the cerebral cortex that expresses somatostatin (sst). The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: 'Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization', dataset: 'Supercluster: MGE-derived interneurons', Author Categories: 'CrossArea_subclass', cluster Sst.\")\n35384:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30001424\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4072027 \"SOM+ inhibitory interneuron (Homo sapiens)\")\n35386:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30001424\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4072027 \"somatostatin-expressing inhibitory interneuron (Homo sapiens)\")\n35389:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4072027 \"sst GABAergic interneuron (Homo sapiens)\")\n35394:# Class: obo:CL_4072029 (pvalb GABAergic interneuron (Homo sapiens))\n35396:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4072029 \"pvalb interneuron (Homo sapiens)\")\n35397:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27477017\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/9c63201d-bfd9-41a8-bbbc-18d947556f3d.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072029 \"A transcriptomically distinct GABAergic interneuron with a soma located in a cerebral cortex and it expresses Parvalbumin. The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: 'Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization', dataset: 'Supercluster: MGE-derived interneurons', Author Categories: 'CrossArea_subclass', cluster Pvalb.\")\n35403:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4072029 \"pvalb GABAergic interneuron (Homo sapiens)\")\n35407:# Class: obo:CL_4072031 (sst chodl GABAergic interneuron (Homo sapiens))\n35409:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4072031 \"sst chodl interneuron (Homo sapiens)\")\n35410:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15845086\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31209381\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33372656\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/9c63201d-bfd9-41a8-bbbc-18d947556f3d.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072031 \"A transcriptomically distinct sst GABAergic interneuron that also expresses Chodl. These neurons are rare and correspond to the only known interneurons with long-range projection. The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: 'Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization', dataset: 'Supercluster: MGE-derived interneurons', Author Categories: 'CrossArea_subclass', clusters Sst Chodl.\")\n35414:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33372656\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4072031 \"long-range GABAergic interneuron (Homo sapiens)\")\n35416:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.11165918\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4072031 \"The marker set NPY can identify the Human cell type sst chodl GABAergic interneuron in the neocortex with a confidence of 0.894026187 (NS-Forest FBeta value).\")\n35417:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4072031 \"sst chodl GABAergic interneuron (Homo sapiens)\")\n35422:# Class: obo:CL_4072032 (VIP GABAergic interneuron (Homo sapiens))\n35424:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4072032 \"VIP interneuron (Homo sapiens)\")\n35425:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33186530\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/e4ddac12-f48f-4455-8e8d-c2a48a683437.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072032 \"A transcriptomically distinct GABAergic neuron that expresses the vasoactive intestinal polypeptide and that has its soma located in the forebrain. The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: 'Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization', dataset: 'Supercluster: CGE-derived interneurons', Author Categories: 'CrossArea_subclass', cluster Vip.\")\n35429:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26420784\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31210267\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33794534\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35221922\") terms:description obo:CL_4072032 \"This neuronal type is distinguished by its heterogeneous morphology and electrophysiological characteristics  (Pronneke et al., 2015,2020; Apicella and Marchionni, 2022). Variations in morphology and firing patterns are observed in human VIP interneurons. In a study by Lee et al., 2023, four distinct subtypes of VIP neurons were identified, each exhibiting unique morphologies, soma locations, and electrophysiological properties. These subtypes are defined according to their transcriptomic markers: LBH-VIP and CCD184-VIP, both of which display a bipolar morphology with axons and dendrites extending across cortical layers; and SY16-VIP and ADAMTSL1-VIP, characterized by a dendritic arbor that spreads horizontally within the same layer as the soma (Lee et al., 2023). Disruption or malfunction of VIP interneuron is implicated in neurodevelopmental disorders such as Rett Syndrome and Dravet Syndrome (Goff and Goldberg 2021).\")\n35436:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.11165918\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4072032 \"The marker set VIP can identify the Human cell type VIP GABAergic interneuron in the neocortex with a confidence of 0.855531344 (NS-Forest FBeta value).\")\n35437:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4072032 \"VIP GABAergic interneuron (Homo sapiens)\")\n35443:# Class: obo:CL_4072034 (lamp5 GABAergic interneuron (Homo sapiens))\n35445:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4072034 \"Lamp5 interneuron (Homo sapiens)\")\n35446:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30382198\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/e4ddac12-f48f-4455-8e8d-c2a48a683437.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072034 \"A transcriptomically distinct GABAergic neuron located in the cerebral cortex that expresses Lamp5. The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: 'Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization', dataset: 'Supercluster: CGE-derived interneurons', Author Categories: 'CrossArea_subclass', clusters Lamp5.\")\n35452:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.11165918\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4072034 \"The marker set LINC00298, KIT can identify the Human cell type lamp5 GABAergic interneuron in the neocortex with a confidence of 0.814687838 (NS-Forest FBeta value).\")\n35453:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4072034 \"lamp5 GABAergic interneuron (Homo sapiens)\")\n35458:# Class: obo:CL_4072035 (sncg GABAergic interneuron (Homo sapiens))\n35460:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4072035 \"sncg interneuron (Homo sapiens)\")\n35461:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33186530\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/e4ddac12-f48f-4455-8e8d-c2a48a683437.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072035 \"A transcriptomically distinct GABAergic neuron located in the cerebral cortex that expresses Gamma-synuclein. The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: 'Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization', dataset: 'Supercluster: CGE-derived interneurons', Author Categories: 'CrossArea_subclass', clusters Sncg.\")\n35468:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.11165918\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4072035 \"The marker set RXRG, THSD7B can identify the Human cell type sncg GABAergic interneuron in the neocortex with a confidence of 0.628943702 (NS-Forest FBeta value).\")\n35469:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4072035 \"sncg GABAergic interneuron (Homo sapiens)\")\n35475:# Class: obo:CL_4072036 (PAX6 GABAergic interneuron (Homo sapiens))\n35477:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4072036 \"Pax6 interneuron (Homo sapiens)\")\n35478:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/e4ddac12-f48f-4455-8e8d-c2a48a683437.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072036 \"A transcriptomically distinct GABAergic neuron located in the cerebral cortex that expresses the transcript PAX6. The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: 'Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization', dataset: 'Supercluster: CGE-derived interneurons', Author Categories: 'CrossArea_subclass', clusters PAX\")\n35482:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.11165918\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4072036 \"The marker set RELN, HCRTR2 can identify the Human cell type PAX6 GABAergic interneuron in the neocortex with a confidence of 0.724125093 (NS-Forest FBeta value).\")\n35483:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4072036 \"PAX6 GABAergic interneuron (Homo sapiens)\")\n35634:# Class: obo:CL_4072046 (pvalb chandelier GABAergic interneuron (Homo sapiens))\n35636:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4072046 \"chandelier PV interneuron (Homo sapiens)\")\n35637:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27477017\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/9c63201d-bfd9-41a8-bbbc-18d947556f3d.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072046 \"A transcriptomically definined GABAergic interneuron of the human pallium.  These cells correspond to the classically defined pvalb chandelier neuron type. The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: 'Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization', dataset: 'Supercluster: CGE-derived interneurons', Author Categories: 'CrossArea_subclass', clusters Chandelier.\")\n35643:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4072046 \"chandelier pvalb GABAergic interneuron (Homo sapiens)\")\n35646:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.11165918\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4072046 \"The marker set GPR149, CA8 can identify the Human cell type chandelier pvalb GABAergic cortical interneuron in the neocortex with a confidence of 0.799748111 (NS-Forest FBeta value).\")\n35647:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4072046 \"pvalb chandelier GABAergic interneuron (Homo sapiens)\")\n35652:# Class: obo:CL_4072102 (Purkinje layer interneuron)\n35654:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35803588\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072102 \"A type of GABAergic interneuron residing in the Purkinje cell layer of the cerebellar cortex.\")\n35657:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4072102 \"Purkinje layer interneuron\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
