ances such as epinephrine, norepinephrine, dopamine, serotonin, enkephalin, somatostatin, neurotensin, and substance P, the actions of which may affect contiguous cells, nearby groups of cells, or distant cells, thus functioning as local or systemic hormones. The name is an acronym for amine precursor uptake and decarboxylation cell.\")\n8688:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000570 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000710 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000001024) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:GO_0001820 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002339 obo:UBERON_0001009))) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:GO_0036161 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002339 obo:UBERON_0001009)))))\n8750:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9505449\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000577 \"A subtype of enteroendocrine cells found in the gastrointestinal mucosa, particularly in the glands of pyloric antrum; duodenum; and ileum. These cell type secretes serotonin and some neurotransmitters including enkephalins and substance P. Their secretory granules stain readily with silver (argentaffin stain).\")\n8785:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000580 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000776 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:CL_0017502) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:GO_0042582) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:PR_000001944) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:PR_000005307) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:PR_000005310) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:PR_000009725) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:PR_000009978) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:PR_000010543) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:CL_4030045 obo:GO_0070820) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:CL_4030046 obo:PR_000001483) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000001012) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000001456) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000001892) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000001932) ObjectSomeValu